---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import { getPublicEmail, siteConfig } from "../config/site";

const { address } = getPublicEmail();
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Angel Bulldogs"
  description="How Angel Bulldogs uses inquiry, contact, and newsletter information on angelbulldogs.com."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <PageHero
    title="Privacy Policy"
    lede="This page describes how Angel Bulldogs uses information you choose to send through this website."
  />
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose measure">
      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Angel Bulldogs is a small French Bulldog program based in {siteConfig.location}. This website
        is a static site: it does not run visitor accounts, a public applicant portal, or a site-owned
        database of form submissions.
      </p>

      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <p>When you send a puppy inquiry, we ask for:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Name</li>
        <li>Email address</li>
        <li>City and state</li>
        <li>Which puppy interests you (or an undecided / future-litter choice)</li>
        <li>Preferred timing</li>
        <li>What you are looking for (family companion, breeding-rights discussion, or not sure yet)</li>
        <li>Optional phone number</li>
        <li>Optional message</li>
        <li>Your acknowledgement that the inquiry is not a reservation</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The general contact form collects your name, email, topic, optional puppy selection, and
        message. The footer newsletter collects only the email address you submit there.
      </p>
      <p>
        Please do not include a street address, payment details, or other sensitive financial
        information in website forms.
      </p>

      <h2>How inquiry and contact messages are delivered</h2>
      <p>
        Puppy inquiry and contact forms are delivered through Formspree using public form endpoints
        configured for this site. Messages are sent so the Angel Bulldogs team can reply using the
        contact details you provide. We use inquiry information to respond and discuss puppy
        placement. A successful inquiry is not an approved application, reservation, or purchase
        contract.
      </p>

      <h2>Newsletter</h2>
      <p>
        The availability newsletter is separate and voluntary. Submitting a puppy inquiry or contact
        message does not subscribe you to the newsletter. Newsletter signups use Brevo (Sendinblue)
        when that public form endpoint is configured.
      </p>

      <h2>What this site does not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>It does not sell your personal information.</li>
        <li>It does not create a public profile or login for applicants.</li>
        <li>It does not process payments on this website.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        {
          address ? (
            <>
              Questions about this policy or a submission you made can be sent by email to{" "}
              <a href={`mailto:${address}`}>{address}</a>.
            </>
          ) : (
            <>
              Questions about this policy or a submission you made can be sent through the{" "}
              <a href="/contact">Contact</a> page.
            </>
          )
        }
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/contact">Contact Angel Bulldogs</a>
        {" · "}
        <a href="/application">Puppy Inquiry</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose h2 {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--color-cocoa);
  }

  .prose p,
  .prose li {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .prose ul {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .prose li + li {
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
  }
</style>
